msgctxt "#32144"
msgid "Automatically sync collection art"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32145"
msgid "Keeps the poster, fanart, logo, banner and other art of Kodi's movie sets in step with Chronicle. Chronicle remembers what each device has been given, so this only compares the collections that changed since, and Kodi is touched only where a set's art really differs. Nothing is written to the \"Movie set information folder\" any more. On by default."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32146"
msgid "Sync Collection Art Now"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32147"
msgid "Updated {0} collection(s){1}"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32148"
msgid "Runs one collection art sync pass immediately, regardless of the automatic settings above. Useful right after changing a collection's art in Chronicle you want reflected in Kodi without waiting for the next scheduled sync."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32149"
msgid "Sync with Chronicle after each library scan"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32150"
msgid "After any video library scan finishes -- Kodi's own automatic one or your own manual \"Update Library\" -- runs the watch history and ratings sync (which also corrects any movie whose details or art disagree with Chronicle, and finishes what a quick scan left for later) and then the collection art sync. Each changes only what differs from Chronicle. On by default."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32151"
msgid "Scanning the video library..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32152"
msgid "Cleaning the video library..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32153"
msgid "Waiting for the library scan to finish before {0}"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32154"
msgid "Scanning"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32155"
msgid "Quick scan: add movies first, fill in details afterwards"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32156"
msgid "While Kodi scans, only adds each movie with Chronicle's text details (title, plot, cast, ratings, artwork links). Writing poster/fanart files next to the movies and the watched/rating/resume sync are skipped during the scan and done by the passes that run right after it (the watch history and ratings sync, then the collection art sync). Makes scanning a large number of new movies many times faster. On by default."
msgstr ""

